# Build context exclusions for `docker build` / `docker compose build`.
#
# The Dockerfile does `COPY . .`, so anything left here is baked into
# an image layer and ships with it - including to Docker Hub, which
# .github/workflows/dockerhub.yml pushes to on every push to master.
# Secrets and local state must not be in that layer.
#
# The project is `virtual` in uv.lock, so `uv sync --frozen` never
# builds it - only pyproject.toml and uv.lock are needed at sync time,
# and musicbot/, config/, run.py and assets/ at runtime. Nothing below
# is required for either.

# Secrets and per-host state. .env is the reason this file exists:
# it holds BOT_TOKEN, and without this it lands in the image.
.env
config/cookies/cookies.txt

# Runtime data - the live guild settings DB and the pickled playlists
# are the host's, not the image's. Both are bind-mounted or volumed in
# by docker-compose.yaml at run time.
settings.db
data/
backup/
log.txt

# Virtualenv. Besides being ~54 MB, a venv built on the host is
# wrong for the image - a Windows one has Scripts/*.exe and absolute
# host paths, and uv would be syncing on top of it.
.venv/
venv/

# VCS. `d!update` shells out to `git pull`, but the image has no git
# binary installed, so nothing in the container can use this anyway.
.git/
.gitignore

# Python build/bytecode artifacts. **/ prefixes are required: unlike
# .gitignore, a .dockerignore pattern is matched against the whole
# relative path, so a bare `__pycache__` would only exclude one at the
# context root and miss musicbot/__pycache__ and friends.
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.egg-info
build/
dist/
*.spec

# Editor, tooling and agent scratch
.idea/
.vscode/
.cache/
.claude/
.superpowers/
.mcp.json
.ignore
graft/

# Docs, CI and dev-only trees - not used at runtime
.github/
docs/
tests/
heroku-legacy/
CLAUDE.md
README.md
LICENSE
.pre-commit-config.yaml

# Not needed inside the image: compose is what builds/runs it, and
# the Dockerfile is already applied by the time the context is read.
docker-compose.yaml
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
